       "type": "text",
       "text": "I entered the order as ORD-0001: ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth four times daily, with a note to give it with food or milk.\n\nThe total is 3,200 mg per day, which is the maximum labeled daily dose. That is appropriate for your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies. Here are some things to consider with your team:\n\n- **Duration:** Use the lowest effective dose for the shortest time. You may want to set a stop date or a reassessment point.\n- **GI protection:** Ask whether your patient needs a PPI. The risk is higher with a high dose, older age, a history of ulcers, or use of steroids, anticoagulants, or SSRIs.\n- **Monitoring:** Watch blood pressure, kidney function, and signs of GI bleeding if the course runs longer than a few days.\n- **Other NSAIDs:** Make sure the patient isn't also taking aspirin or other NSAIDs."
      }
